# No bare “terminate” in public copy

Residents hear **terminate** as movie-kill slang, not HR or contract jargon. Do not put bare `terminate` / `terminated` / `termination` in this site’s voice on published pages (`*.html`, speech JSON, widget intro text, news notes).

## Employment

| Ban (our voice) | Write instead |
|---|---|
| “was terminated,” “officer terminated,” “terminated them,” “pending termination” | **fired**, **resigned**, or (rare) **terminated their employment** |
| Lookup Outcome saying “Terminated” | **fired** (JSON may keep `Terminated` for filters/tallies) |

## Contracts / municipal exits

| Ban (our voice) | Write instead |
|---|---|
| “terminate the contract,” “terminate vote,” “terminate resolution,” “this is a terminate” | **end**, **cancel**, **drop**, **cut**, **non-renew**, **vote to end** |
| “Pause, not a reported terminate” | “Pause, not a reported cancel.” / “Cameras stay; no end vote yet.” |

## OK to leave

- Direct quotes from outlets, officials, or contracts (`“removed upon the termination or expiration of this Agreement”`)
- Outlet titles and `href` / archive URLs that contain the word
- Catalog JSON machine values (`Outcome_Bucket`, action enums) when the **public** label is already rewritten
- Maintainer-only notes in `.cursor/rules/` and git comments

## Check

Before finishing public copy, scan the **diff** for `terminat`. If it is this site speaking, rewrite it in the same task.
